      ":question/id": "dd1487e8-c1a1-5fdc-9df5-1c7be4d8489d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given $q=⟨12,1,-11⟩$ and $r=⟨-4,4,3⟩.$\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n$q\\cdot r=\\,$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor these vectors, we have $q=⟨12,1,-11⟩$ and $r=⟨-4,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =12\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 4+(-11)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-48+4-33 \\\\  & =-77.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
